Title: Night Shift
Author: Script Glow

INT. HOSPITAL BREAK ROOM - NIGHT

Fluorescent hum. A vending machine glows. DANA, an ER nurse in her thirties, eats cold noodles standing up. The door opens. MICHAEL, her younger brother, rain on his jacket, hovers in the doorway.

MICHAEL
They said you'd be in here.

DANA
They shouldn't have.

MICHAEL
I told them I was family.

DANA
You are. That's the problem.

MICHAEL
Hi, Dana.

DANA
Four years, Michael. You don't get a "hi."

MICHAEL
What do I get?

DANA
Ten minutes. I'm on break.

He sits. She doesn't.

MICHAEL
You look tired.

DANA
It's three in the morning and I work in an emergency room. Tired is the uniform.

MICHAEL
I called Mom's number last week. It's disconnected.

DANA
She moved in with me. In March.

MICHAEL
In March. Nobody told me.

DANA
Who was I supposed to tell? You changed your number twice.

MICHAEL
I know.

DANA
You don't know. You weren't here. I found her on the kitchen floor, Michael. I did the compressions myself. On my own mother.

MICHAEL
(quietly)
Is she okay?

DANA
She's okay. She forgets things. She asks about you every Sunday.

MICHAEL
What do you tell her?

DANA
That you're busy. That you're doing well. Are you?

MICHAEL
I've been sober eleven months.

She finally looks at him.

DANA
Eleven months.

MICHAEL
I have the chip. I didn't want to come until I had the chip.

DANA
You could have called at six months. At one month.

MICHAEL
I didn't trust myself to still have it by the time you picked up.

DANA
That's not fair.

MICHAEL
I know it's not. None of it's fair to you. That's why I'm here.

DANA
Why now? Why tonight?

MICHAEL
Because you work nights, and I figured you couldn't slam a door in a hospital.

She almost laughs. Catches it.

DANA
Don't do that.

MICHAEL
Do what?

DANA
Be funny. I'm still angry.

MICHAEL
You can be both. You always were.

A pager buzzes on her hip. She checks it.

DANA
I have to go.

MICHAEL
Can I see her? Mom?

DANA
Sunday. Two o'clock. She naps after three.

MICHAEL
I'll be there at two.

DANA
Be there at one forty-five. She likes people early.

MICHAEL
One forty-five.

She heads for the door. Stops.

DANA
Michael. Bring the chip.

MICHAEL
Why?

DANA
Because I want to see it.

She goes.
